  <h1>How to Make Turkey Jerky</h1>

  <div class="answer-box">
    <p>To make turkey jerky, trim and slice lean turkey breast 1/4 inch thick, marinate 4–12 hours, then heat the strips to an internal temperature of <strong>165°F</strong> before drying at <strong>160°F for 4–6 hours</strong>. Turkey is leaner than beef and easy to make low-sodium, but the 165°F pre-heat is essential — poultry carries a Salmonella risk that most home dehydrators cannot destroy on their own.</p>
  </div>

  <ContentImage src="/images/turkey-jerky.webp" alt="Homemade turkey jerky strips on a dark board, dried and lightly glossy" eager={true} />

